@startuml 013-memory-starvation
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam defaultFontName "Arial"

title Memory Footprint Mapping - O(1) Bounded Architecture vs O(N) Starvation

box "Linux System Host Layout" #White
participant "Physical Disk\n(512MB Asset)" as Disk
participant "Operating System\nKernel Page Cache" as Kernel
participant "Python Process RAM\nStaging Buffer" as RAM
participant "Network Socket\nInterface Card" as NIC
end box

note over RAM #LightGray
  Invariant Resource Framework Allocation Boundary (Max ~77MB Peak)
  Contains: Python Interpreter runtime + compiled core libraries
end note

loop Over 131,072 Iterations [512MB File / 4KB Transfer Page]
    Disk -> Kernel: pull memory page via DMA
    Kernel -> RAM: copy bounded 4096-Byte window (CHUNK_SIZE)
    activate RAM
    note over RAM: Inline Processing Layer:\n1. Apply AES-256-CTR encryption\n2. Update cumulative SHA-256 state
    RAM -> Kernel: transmit encrypted ciphertext window via sendall()
    deactivate RAM
    Kernel -> NIC: flash data block to physical network medium
end

note over RAM #LightGreen
  Result: Memory Footprint remains flat at O(1) throughout execution.
  Immune to data volume capacity scaling.
end note
@enduml
